      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"strategic angle\" idea, but if I write that it's \"on the cusp of definitive proof\" and then the reviewers dig into the data and see a 0.06, they might think we're trying to hide something. They're pretty strict about that. Is there any way we can frame the results themselves to be more convincing without just relying on \"trends\" and \"plausibility\"? Like, can we present the data in a way that makes the significance feel more established?",
