      "content": "You can strategically frame the data by focusing heavily on the magnitude of the effect size, rather than solely on the p-value. A large effect size, even with a borderline p-value, signals a clinically meaningful difference that warrants further, immediate investigation. Furthermore, highlight the consistency across different subgroups within the trial; this consistency acts as a powerful, albeit indirect, indicator of reliability. This approach showcases scientific rigor while tactfully managing the statistical nuance.",
